  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The long lobes of this cultivar are deep red or purple red in the spring and early summer. They gradually turn a reddish green or bronze green. Crimson color tones dominate in the fall. The leaves do not hold their red color as well as those of 'Atrolineare'. They have mostly five lobes, occasionally three or seven lobes, and are 5-7 cm long and about 6 cm wide. Each lobe is up to 6 mm wide and has slightly serrated margins. The petioles are about 3 cm long. This cultivar grows more slowly than"
  },
